## ABSTRACT

This project presents **accsoft**, a double-entry accounting system built primarily inside a PostgreSQL database. The system stores all accounting data in Supabase PostgreSQL and calculates every financial report using recursive SQL common table expressions (CTEs), standard aggregations, and database views. A lightweight Python frontend built with Streamlit connects to Supabase, retrieves live report data, and displays it in the browser. The application is hosted online at no cost using Streamlit Community Cloud and GitHub. The architecture demonstrates that complete accounting logic — including multi-level account hierarchies, trial balance, income statement, balance sheet, reconciliation, cash flow, general ledger, accounts receivable aging, accounts payable aging, vendor statements, and customer statements — can be implemented almost entirely in SQL, with the frontend acting only as a display layer. This approach aligns with the project goal of maximizing SQL expertise while minimizing frontend complexity.

