## 1. INTRODUCTION

### 1.1 Background

Modern small-business accounting software such as Xero and QuickBooks provides rich functionality but requires significant infrastructure and licensing costs. For academic purposes, a simplified yet functionally complete accounting system can demonstrate core computer science competencies — database design, recursive query optimization, cloud deployment, and web application development — without requiring expensive platforms or complex frontend frameworks.

The author has professional experience in accounting software and strong expertise in SQL. This project leverages that strength by placing the majority of business logic inside the database layer.

### 1.2 Project Overview

Accsoft is a web-based double-entry accounting system. Data is entered into Supabase PostgreSQL tables. Financial reports are generated dynamically through SQL views. A Streamlit application queries these views and presents live results. The entire stack operates on free-tier cloud services.

