## 13. CONCLUSION

This project demonstrates that a functional double-entry accounting system can be built with SQL as the primary engineering tool. By placing recursive hierarchy logic, balance roll-ups, and financial report calculations inside PostgreSQL views, the system achieves clean separation of concerns: the database handles all accounting rules, while the Python frontend merely displays results. The deployment uses entirely free services, making it accessible for academic demonstration and small-business prototyping. The system successfully produces a Trial Balance, Income Statement, Balance Sheet, Reconciliation, Cash Flow, General Ledger, and full Accounts Receivable / Accounts Payable aging reports from live data.

