## 15. APPENDICES

### Appendix A: Master Account Hierarchy SQL Pattern

```sql
WITH RECURSIVE hh AS (
    SELECT
        account_category,
        account_type,
        account_code,
        1 AS sorting,
        account_name,
        account_sub1,
        account_name::text AS path,
        ARRAY[account_code] AS path_codes
    FROM chart_of_accounts
    WHERE account_sub1 IS NULL

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        coa.account_category,
        coa.account_type,
        coa.account_code,
        hh.sorting + 1,
        coa.account_name,
        coa.account_sub1,
        CONCAT(hh.path, ' > ', coa.account_name) AS path,
        hh.path_codes || coa.account_code
    FROM chart_of_accounts AS coa
    JOIN hh ON coa.account_sub1 = hh.account_name
    AND NOT (coa.account_code = ANY(hh.path_codes))
)
SELECT * FROM hh ORDER BY path;
```

### Appendix B: Core Report Views

The views `view_account_summary`, `view_balance_sheet`, `view_trial_balance`, `view_reconciliation`, `view_income_statement`, `view_full_financial_statement`, `view_chart_of_accounts`, and `view_journal_register` are created in Supabase SQL Editor. Each view queries the recursive hierarchy and journal aggregations described in Section 7.

